Upload a file from your client into the in-world filesystem.

usage: @fput <path>

Uploads a file chosen in the client to the given absolute VFS path, creating
or overwriting it. Parent directories are created as needed. This is how you
bring a source or a prebuilt image in from your machine.

This command is only available from the web client. On a terminal client it
reports that it is unsupported; use @fedit to author a text file in place
instead.

The path must be an absolute VFS path made of letters, digits, '/', '.', '-',
and '_'. Wizard only.

Example:
  @fput /src/util.kp
      Pick a local file to store at /src/util.kp through the web client.

See also @fget, @fedit, @fcat, @fls.
